  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Feddan Productive Farming Zones</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In response to the humanitarian crisis in Sudan, the Feddan Community Gardens initiative, led by the UNDP and partners, aims to establish small productive farming zones to bolster food security and economic resilience among Internally Displaced People&apos;s (IDPs) and host communities. The project focuses on integrated farming to provide employment, enhance local food production, and offer sustainable solutions to the challenges posed by conflict and displacement. Key activities include poultry and livestock farming, feed and Azolla cultivation, and organic waste recycling. The pilot phase will involve community engagement, capacity building, and continuous monitoring to ensure the project&apos;s adaptability and long-term success. This initiative represents a strategic effort to cultivate a self-reliant and robust community capable of overcoming the current crisis and future challenges.</narrative>
  </description>
